// Invalid: workflow terminals whose DECLARED payload contract no payload can
// take. spec/language.md: a terminal payload contract is either a class (a
// field block) or a scalar type.
//
// The refusal used to fire only from the rule that COMPLETES the terminal, so
// a workflow that declared the contract and never completed that terminal was
// accepted, contract and all — and `error` here is never failed, `extra` never
// completed. The declaration is the mistake; the completion was only where it
// happened to be noticed. D14, spec/diagnostic-quality-tracker.md.
workflow DeclaredUnsupportedPayloadContract

output result Outcome
output extra Outcome[]
failure error Trouble?

class Outcome {
  note string
}

class Trouble {
  reason string
}

rule r
  when started
=> {
  complete result { note "x" }
}
